  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220B)=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =\\frac{x+3}{3x-5} \\\\ 3(3x-5) & =2(x+3) \\\\ 9x-15 & =2x+6 \\\\ 7x & =21 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x-5=3(3)-5=4, \\\\ AC & =x+3=3+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
